          imageCaption: `Latin America: ~660M people, 33 countries from Mexico through Patagonia. Pre-Columbian civilizations: Maya (250-900 CE classical peak, 6M+ Maya speakers today), Aztec/Mexica (1325-1521, Tenochtitlan), Inca (1438-1533, 40,000+ km roads), Toltecs/Olmecs/Zapotec/Mixtec/Chimú/Mochica/Wari/Tiwanaku, Caribs/Arawaks, Mapuche, Quechua/Aymara, Amazonian nations. Pre-Columbian population ~50-100M+; ~80-95% loss after ~150 years colonization (diseases + violence). Transatlantic slave trade: ~5M enslaved to Latin America (Brazil ~4.9M, vs US ~388,000). Independence wars 1810-1825 (Bolívar, San Martín, Hidalgo); state borders established but underlying social structures unchanged. US Monroe Doctrine 1823, US-Mexico War 1846-1848, Spanish-American War 1898.`,
